@mgirlich do you have time to review a few dbplyr PRs?

When a `src` is created from a DBI-compliant connection, it gets the S3 class `src_TYPEConnection`.  However, a DBI connection can extend, and thus inherit, from other DBI classes and thus the `src_` type should reflect these.  In my case, my [`doltr` package](https://github.com/ecohealthalliance/doltr) connects to Dolt databases, which are MySQL/MariaDB compatible and thus `DoltConnection` extends `MariaDBConnection`.  The `dm` package [queries the class of `src_` objects to determine database type](https://github.com/cynkra/dm/blob/main/R/db-helpers.R#L67-L70), but since `dplyr` doesn't include class extensions when creating `src_` types, this compatibility is invisible.

This PR changes the construction of `src_dbi` objects so they inherit all the types of DBI connections they extend.

